</section>
<section id="S6.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S6.SS4.4" class="ltx_text">VI-D</span> </span><span id="S6.SS4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Evaluations on Multi-Modal Controls</span></h3>

<div id="S6.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we evaluate the effectiveness of multi-modal controls, including intrinsic channels, reference images, and text prompts.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qualitative Results.</span>
As in Fig. <a href="#S6.F5" title="Fig. 5 ‣ VI-B Metrics ‣ VI Experimental Results ‣ X2Video: Adapting Diffusion Models for Multimodal Controllable Neural Video Rendering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we first show the impact of intrinsic channels on affecting the color, material, and texture of the generated contents. In the <math id="S6.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1^{\text{st}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>1</mn><mtext>st</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1^{\text{st}}</annotation></semantics></math> example, the floor color is changed and reflections are eliminated by adjusting albedo, roughness, and metallicity.
The <math id="S6.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{\text{nd}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mtext>nd</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{\text{nd}}</annotation></semantics></math> example illustrates modifications to the texture and color of the wall.
Then in the <math id="S6.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3^{\text{rd}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>3</mn><mtext>rd</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3^{\text{rd}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>4</mn><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> examples, the reference image is used to restore the dropped or masked intrinsic information, as emphasized within the red frames.
After that, in the <math id="S6.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>5</mn><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>6</mn><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> examples, the irradiance channel is omitted, and text prompts are employed to indicate the overall color environment and global lighting.
Lastly, in the <math id="S6.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>7</mn><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>8</mn><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> examples, text prompts are used to control and modify the color and material of specific masked local regions.
The results demonstrate the effectiveness of our multi-modal conditions on controlling and editing the appearance of both global and local regions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Quantitative Results.</span>
As shown in Tab. <a href="#S6.T3" title="TABLE III ‣ VI-C Evaluations on Intrinsic-Guided Video Rendering ‣ VI Experimental Results ‣ X2Video: Adapting Diffusion Models for Multimodal Controllable Neural Video Rendering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III</span></a>, the results obtained using only intrinsic channels are presented as the baseline in the <math id="S6.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1^{\text{st}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>1</mn><mtext>st</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1^{\text{st}}</annotation></semantics></math> row.
Then in the <math id="S6.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{\text{nd}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mtext>nd</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{\text{nd}}</annotation></semantics></math> row, we either mask the albedo, metallic, and roughness of three random objects, or omit the irradiance channels, referring to ”Mask A<math id="S6.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|</annotation></semantics></math>M<math id="S6.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|</annotation></semantics></math>R” and ”Drop Irrad.”. The observed decline across all metrics demonstrates the significance of the intrinsic channels in providing essential information for accurate outputs.
Following this, we introduce text prompts and reference images separately to compensate for the missing information caused by the masked or omitted intrinsic channels. As shown in the <math id="S6.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3^{\text{rd}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>3</mn><mtext>rd</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3^{\text{rd}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>4</mn><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> row, these additional controls lead to improvements across all metrics, which demonstrates the efficacy of our Hybrid Self-Attention and Masked Cross-Attention in utilizing reference and text conditions effectively.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.08530v1/abl_mask.png" id="S6.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/103;" width="476" height="103" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 7: </span>Ablation study on Masked Cross-Attention. Our Masked Cross-Attention can better apply the text prompts into specified local regions with more accurate colors.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
